# UE5 build artifacts
Binaries/
Intermediate/
Saved/
DerivedDataCache/
Build/

# Plugin build artifacts
Plugins/*/Binaries/
Plugins/*/Intermediate/

# Dead vendored library — pre-FSocket FSDSPlugin used rpclib for the RPC
# server, but the current implementation is built on UE's FSocket /
# TcpListener (see Plugins/FSDSPlugin/Source/FSDSPlugin/Private/RPC/
# FSDSRpcServer.cpp). The Build.cs no longer references rpclib and no
# source file #includes from it. Older clones may still have a 14 MB
# ThirdParty/rpclib/ checkout on disk — keep git from picking it up.
Plugins/FSDSPlugin/ThirdParty/

# IDE files
.vs/
.vsconfig
*.sln
*.vcxproj*
.vscode/

# Xcode / Mac project files (generated by GenerateProjectFiles.sh)
*.xcworkspace/
*.xcodeproj/

# Python virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Frontend build / dev-server caches (Mission Control is Vite)
node_modules/
.vite/
dist/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Compiled content
*.BI
*.BI2

# ROS2 workspace build artifacts
ros2/build/
ros2/install/
ros2/log/

# Binary content assets tracked via Git LFS (*.uasset, *.umap)
.env

# Claude internal files
.claude/

# Packaged builds
Packaged/

# Generated track files and runtime state
Content/tracks/*.csv
Content/tracks/.ifssim_state.json

# UE5 editor scratch — *_BuiltData.uasset is regenerated lighting / nav
# data the editor saves alongside its .umap. We don't track it (its
# sibling .umap content already has all the source authoring info), so
# it just sits in everyone's `git status` after launching the editor.
*_BuiltData.uasset

# Documents (not source)
*.pdf

# IFS-08 spec source-of-truth dumps from internal teams (vehicle
# dynamics master sheet, autonomous steering design docs, SolidWorks
# CAD models, FEA results). Each ~30-170 MB of binary content;
# committing would explode the repo. Local-only: re-drop into docs/
# from the team's shared drive when needed. PR comments and
# docs/archive/ summaries cite the relevant numbers (wheelbase,
# turning radius, pinion radius, etc.) so the reference content is
# discoverable without the binaries themselves.
docs/MODEL_IFS_08/
docs/Steering_DV_Sandra/

# Recorded ROS2 bags — large binary sqlite DBs, not source.
# `tools/bags/` is the historical location; `bags/` (repo root) is the
# 2026-05-11+ convention used by the offline analysis flow (the bag
# captures land here when copied out of the dv_pipeline_stack container).
tools/bags/
bags/

# Auto-generated tracks from tools/random-track-generator. Each run
# overwrites Content/tracks/random_track.csv; staging an empty/stale
# version in git just confuses the track validator (and ships a
# phantom track in package_mac.sh's CSV copy). Real generated tracks
# are renamed by the operator before commit.
Content/tracks/random_track.csv

# Per-developer docker-compose override. Compose auto-merges this on
# top of docker-compose.yml when present. The committed compose is
# the source of truth and should work on every supported OS as-is
# (PR-#482 brought TCP-LiDAR back, so no per-OS override is needed).
# This entry exists so individual developers can keep local-only
# tweaks — bind-mounting an unreleased ROS package, tightening a
# memory limit on a smaller dev machine, alternate host IPs —
# without committing them.
docker-compose.override.yml

# Release archives produced by package_mac.sh / package_windows.sh
# (Saved/StagedBuilds/ zipped up). Multi-hundred-MB binary blobs,
# not source; uploaded to GitHub Releases via `gh release create`
# at tag time.
dist/

# Compiled odometry_filter pybind module (rebuild: tools/sim_benchmark/build_native_filter.sh)
tools/sim_benchmark/_native/
